# Runtime state a copy produces: the object store's local root (objectstore.fs),
# created at the path the configuration names when the first object is written,
# and the token signing key the program generates on its first run. Both land
# beside the Go module the program runs from and belong to a deployment, not to
# the source tree.
/server/var/

# The frontend's build outputs, which no checkout commits: the installed
# dependency tree and the built bundle. Everything a build writes under
# server/dist is ignored, so building the frontend leaves the working tree
# clean. server/dist has to hold at least one file for go:embed to compile (the
# Go program embeds dist/), so server/dist/placeholder.txt is tracked -- the one
# file a build never touches, force-added despite this rule. See web/README.md.
/web/node_modules/
/server/dist/

# The compiled server binary: a `go build` (or `go run`'s cached build) run in
# server/ leaves it beside the module, named for the package. It is a build
# artifact, not source.
/server/demo
